# Implementation Roadmap: AI-Driven Development Lifecycle (AIDLC)

*Prepared for Engineering Management | Integrating Polarion, GitHub, Copilot, & Superpowers*

## 1. Executive Summary

This roadmap outlines the strategic transition from a traditional Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) to an AI-Driven Lifecycle (AIDLC). By combining our existing toolchain (Siemens Polarion ALM and GitHub) with AI execution capabilities (GitHub Copilot and the Superpowers methodology via the Model Context Protocol), we can achieve autonomous traceability, test-driven AI development, and strict compliance governance. This document provides the comparative benefits and the step-by-step technical rollout plan.

## 2. Business Value: Before vs. After AIDLC

Implementing this architecture shifts our AI from a simple "code autocomplete" tool into an integrated systems engineer that respects enterprise workflows.

| Capability Area | Current State (Traditional SDLC + Basic AI) | Future State (AIDLC with Superpowers & MCP) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Requirements Context** | Developers manually read Polarion, switch tabs, and copy-paste context into Copilot. High risk of missing nuance. | Copilot directly queries Polarion Work Items via MCP, reading approved specifications and design constraints natively. |
| **Code Quality** | AI generates code blindly. Developers must manually verify if it meets the original business requirement. | Superpowers forces a strict Test-Driven Development (TDD) loop. Code is only committed if it passes agent-authored tests. |
| **Traceability & Compliance** | Manual linking of GitHub commits and Test Runs back to Polarion. Often delayed until audit time. | AI automatically appends Work Item IDs to Git commits and logs passing test results directly to Polarion Test Runs. |
| **Governance** | Human developers can accidentally bypass approval gates or build against unapproved drafts. | The MCP agent is constrained by Polarion permissions and explicitly halted by Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) workflow gates. |

## 3. Architecture & Toolchain Alignment

*   **The Source of Truth:** Siemens Polarion ALM (Requirements, Test Runs, Traceability Matrix).
*   **The Bridge:** Polarion MCP Server (Model Context Protocol). Allows the AI to read and write ALM data securely.
*   **The Source Code:** GitHub (Version Control, Pull Requests, CI/CD).
*   **The AI Executer:** GitHub Copilot (Integrated into IDEs or Workspaces), configured to consume MCP tools.
*   **The Cognitive Framework:** Superpowers Methodology (Injected via System Prompts to force planning, TDD, and debugging loops).

